From 76ccfac00f86c6b47ea0ad4f257b61a907c3d3ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:18:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/50] Bound prompt-logprobs chunks by max_num_reqs

Model Runner V2 computes prompt logprobs in chunks of 1024 rows of
full-vocabulary logits. profile_run's sampler step only materializes one
logits row per request, so with max_num_seqs below 1024 the prompt-logprobs
chunk is larger than anything the memory profile measured, and the KV
cache is sized without it.

Cap the chunk at max_num_reqs rows. Results are unchanged (rows are
independent); deployments with max_num_seqs >= 1024 keep 1024-row chunks.

Cherry-picked from vllm-project/vllm#63564 (fixes #63563).
